From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Chad Cormier Roussel <chadcormierroussel@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 20:26:43 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] FEXInterpreter: HostTSO, for a host that runs the whole VM
 with TSO

MacNeutron's microVM sets Apple's ACTLR_EL1.EnTSO on every vCPU from the host, so a stock guest kernel
(no PR_SET_MEM_MODEL) runs everything with TSO ordering. HostTSO (FEX_HOSTTSO) tells FEX so: it calls
SetHardwareTSOSupport(true) and emits no ordering barriers, as it does after a successful
PR_SET_MEM_MODEL. The guest image sets it only after a boot-time litmus test sees no violation.

x64-bench mem_seq_read under FEX in a VM without TSO: 0.996 s plain, 0.480 s TSOEnabled=0, 0.479 s
HostTSO=1.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 FEXCore/Source/Interface/Config/Config.json.in | 9 +++++++++
 Source/Tools/FEXInterpreter/FEXInterpreter.cpp | 7 +++++++
 2 files changed, 16 insertions(+)

diff --git a/FEXCore/Source/Interface/Config/Config.json.in b/FEXCore/Source/Interface/Config/Config.json.in
index bce7b25..82eeb53 100644
--- a/FEXCore/Source/Interface/Config/Config.json.in
+++ b/FEXCore/Source/Interface/Config/Config.json.in
@@ -651,6 +651,15 @@
           "Highly likely to break any multithreaded application if disabled."
         ]
       },
+      "HostTSO": {
+        "Type": "bool",
+        "Default": "false",
+        "AffectsCodeGen": "true",
+        "Desc": [
+          "The host already runs this process with TSO memory ordering (a VM whose vCPUs have Apple's EnTSO set).",
+          "FEX then emits no ordering barriers."
+        ]
+      },
       "VectorTSOEnabled": {
         "Type": "bool",
         "Default": "false",
diff --git a/Source/Tools/FEXInterpreter/FEXInterpreter.cpp b/Source/Tools/FEXInterpreter/FEXInterpreter.cpp
index 869f946..84ae9dd 100644
--- a/Source/Tools/FEXInterpreter/FEXInterpreter.cpp
+++ b/Source/Tools/FEXInterpreter/FEXInterpreter.cpp
@@ -266,6 +266,13 @@ bool QueryInterpreterInstalled(bool ExecutedWithFD, const FEX::Config::PortableI
 namespace FEX::Kernel {
 namespace TSO {
   void SetupTSOEmulation(FEXCore::Context::Context* CTX) {
+    FEX_CONFIG_OPT(HostTSO, HOSTTSO);
+    if (HostTSO()) {
+      // The host set TSO on every vCPU of this VM (nothing in the guest can switch it), so emulate nothing.
+      CTX->SetHardwareTSOSupport(true);
+      return;
+    }
+
     // Check to see if this is supported.
     auto Result = prctl(PR_GET_MEM_MODEL, 0, 0, 0, 0);
     if (Result == -1) {
